---
import Mark from "@guiferviz/cheese-bytes-video/astro/Mark.astro";
import StorySection from "@guiferviz/cheese-bytes-video/astro/StorySection.astro";
import VideoVisual from "@guiferviz/cheese-bytes-video/astro/VideoVisual.astro";
import { MisraGriesVisual, misraGriesDefinition } from "../components/cave/misra-gries/video/MisraGriesVisual";
---

<StorySection id="question" timeline={(t) => {
    const visual = t.visual("summary", misraGriesDefinition);
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "start", duration: 1.5, ease: "linear", params: { value: 1 } });
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "memory", duration: 2.1, ease: "linear", params: { value: 2 } });
  }}>
  <aside class="notes">
    <p><Mark id="start" />Suppose we throw most of these shapes away. Can we still prove that squares make up more than a third of the stream?</p>
    <p><Mark id="memory" />Counting every kind would work. But as new kinds arrive, that table keeps growing. Can just two counters be useful?</p>
  </aside>
  <VideoVisual id="summary"><MisraGriesVisual initial={{ scene: "hook", step: 0 }} client:only="react" /></VideoVisual>
</StorySection>

<StorySection id="two-slots" timeline={(t) => {
    const visual = t.visual("summary", misraGriesDefinition);
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "square", duration: 1.6, ease: "linear", params: { value: 1 } });
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "circle", duration: 1.6, ease: "linear", params: { value: 2 } });
  }}>
  <aside class="notes">
    <p><Mark id="start" />Let's start with a square and a circle.</p>
    <p><Mark id="square" />Each takes an empty slot, with a count of one.</p>
    <p><Mark id="circle" />A matching arrival would increase its counter. What happens when a new kind finds both slots full?</p>
  </aside>
  <VideoVisual id="summary"><MisraGriesVisual initial={{ scene: "slots", step: 0 }} client:only="react" /></VideoVisual>
</StorySection>

<StorySection id="cancel-three" timeline={(t) => {
    const visual = t.visual("summary", misraGriesDefinition);
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "start", duration: 1.5, ease: "linear", params: { value: 1 } });
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "remove", duration: 2.4, ease: "linear", params: { value: 2 } });
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "tally", duration: 1.5, ease: "linear", params: { value: 3 } });
  }}>
  <aside class="notes">
    <p><Mark id="start" />Then a triangle arrives. No match. No empty slot.</p>
    <p><Mark id="remove" />So we cancel one square, one circle, and the triangle together.</p>
    <p><Mark id="tally" />Three different shapes. We forget which shapes they were, but remember one thing: one group removed.</p>
  </aside>
  <VideoVisual id="summary"><MisraGriesVisual initial={{ scene: "cancel", step: 0 }} client:only="react" /></VideoVisual>
</StorySection>

<StorySection id="one-pass" timeline={(t) => {
    const visual = t.visual("summary", misraGriesDefinition);
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "run", to: "result", ease: "linear", params: { value: 15 } });
  }}>
  <aside class="notes">
    <p><Mark id="start" />Let's rewind and follow these fifteen shapes, from left to right.</p>
    <p><Mark id="run" />Matches add one. Empty slots accept a new shape. Otherwise, three different shapes disappear together.</p>
    <p><Mark id="result" />The summary ends with five squares and one circle. Three groups were removed. But five is not the number of squares that arrived.</p>
  </aside>
  <VideoVisual id="summary"><MisraGriesVisual initial={{ scene: "trace", step: 0 }} client:only="react" /></VideoVisual>
</StorySection>

<StorySection id="bounds" timeline={(t) => {
    const visual = t.visual("summary", misraGriesDefinition);
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "start", duration: 2.1, ease: "linear", params: { value: 1 } });
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "hidden", duration: 2.5, ease: "linear", params: { value: 2 } });
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "interval", duration: 2.4, ease: "linear", params: { value: 3 } });
  }}>
  <aside class="notes">
    <p><Mark id="start" />Those five surviving squares are real. At least five squares arrived.</p>
    <p><Mark id="hidden" />And each removed group contained at most one square. Three groups could hide at most three more.</p>
    <p><Mark id="interval" />Five survived. At most three were lost. So the true count is between five and eight. That is a guarantee, not a guess.</p>
  </aside>
  <VideoVisual id="summary"><MisraGriesVisual initial={{ scene: "bounds", step: 0 }} client:only="react" /></VideoVisual>
</StorySection>

<StorySection id="heavy-hitters" timeline={(t) => {
    const visual = t.visual("summary", misraGriesDefinition);
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "start", duration: 2, ease: "linear", params: { value: 1 } });
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "uncertain", duration: 1.6, ease: "linear", params: { value: 2 } });
  }}>
  <aside class="notes">
    <p><Mark id="start" />Our question was: more than a third? In fifteen shapes, that means more than five.</p>
    <p><Mark id="uncertain" />Our interval still includes five. So we cannot say yes yet. Surviving alone does not answer the question.</p>
  </aside>
  <VideoVisual id="summary"><MisraGriesVisual initial={{ scene: "threshold", step: 0 }} client:only="react" /></VideoVisual>
</StorySection>

<StorySection id="more-memory" timeline={(t) => {
    const visual = t.visual("summary", misraGriesDefinition);
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "run", to: "result", ease: "linear", params: { value: 15 } });
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "result", duration: 2.5, ease: "linear", params: { value: 16 } });
  }}>
  <aside class="notes">
    <p><Mark id="start" />What if we spend one more counter? Replay the same fifteen shapes.</p>
    <p><Mark id="run" />Now it takes four different shapes to cancel. Watch the same stream: just one group is removed.</p>
    <p><Mark id="result" />Six squares survive. At most one was lost. So the true count is between six and seven.</p>
  </aside>
  <VideoVisual id="summary"><MisraGriesVisual initial={{ scene: "replay", step: 0 }} client:only="react" /></VideoVisual>
</StorySection>

<StorySection id="decide" timeline={(t) => {
    const visual = t.visual("summary", misraGriesDefinition);
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "certain", duration: 1.8, ease: "linear", params: { value: 1 } });
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "exact", duration: 0.8, ease: "linear", params: { value: 2 } });
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "recount", to: "answer", ease: "linear", params: { value: 3 } });
  }}>
  <aside class="notes">
    <p><Mark id="start" />Six to seven is entirely above five.</p>
    <p><Mark id="certain" />Yes: squares make up more than a third. This decision needs no second pass.</p>
    <p><Mark id="exact" />We still don't know the exact count.</p>
    <p><Mark id="recount" />If we can read the data again, a second pass gives us seven.</p>
    <p><Mark id="answer" />But our original question is already answered.</p>
  </aside>
  <VideoVisual id="summary"><MisraGriesVisual initial={{ scene: "decide", step: 0 }} client:only="react" /></VideoVisual>
</StorySection>

<StorySection id="tradeoff" timeline={(t) => {
    const visual = t.visual("summary", misraGriesDefinition);
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "bound", duration: 2.4, ease: "linear", params: { value: 1 } });
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "scale", duration: 3.8, ease: "linear", params: { value: 2 } });
  }}>
  <aside class="notes">
    <p><Mark id="start" />This is Misra Gries. With m counters, we cancel groups of m plus one different values.</p>
    <p><Mark id="bound" />Every deletion removes m plus one items, and at most one of any kind. So the error is at most N divided by m plus one, where N is the stream length.</p>
    <p><Mark id="scale" />Ninety nine counters cap that error at one percent of the stream. A guaranteed margin, not a confidence score.</p>
  </aside>
  <VideoVisual id="summary"><MisraGriesVisual initial={{ scene: "general", step: 0 }} client:only="react" /></VideoVisual>
</StorySection>

<StorySection id="closing" holdAfter={10} timeline={(t) => {
    const visual = t.visual("summary", misraGriesDefinition);
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "insight", duration: 1.8, ease: "linear", params: { value: 1 } });
    t.action(visual.advance, { from: "end", duration: 2.4, ease: "linear", params: { value: 2 } });
  }}>
  <aside class="notes">
    <p><Mark id="start" />We started by throwing shapes away.</p>
    <p><Mark id="insight" />The trick was to keep a limit on what could have disappeared.</p>
    <p><Mark id="end" />We may lose the exact count, without losing the answer.</p>
  </aside>
  <VideoVisual id="summary"><MisraGriesVisual initial={{ scene: "closing", step: 0 }} client:only="react" /></VideoVisual>
</StorySection>
